     <h1 class="title" title="Lonavala Hill Station">Lonavala</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/west-india-hill-stations/lonavala-hill-station.jpg" title="Lonavala hill station" alt="Lonavala hill station, hill stations in india, west india hill stations, Lonavala" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> 96 kms from Mumbai, Maharashtra<br />
<b>Area:</b> 215 sq.kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Jewel of the Sahyadri Mountains<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 625m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 30&#176;C - 35&#176;C, Winter 12&#176;C - 15&#176;C<br />
<b>Best time to visit:</b> October to May</p>     
<p>Located in the green hills of <b>Sahyadri</b>, <b>Lonavala</b> is at an altitude of 625 m and is the destination for weekend's most popular <b>Mumbai</b> and <b>Pune</b>. Known as the <b>jewel of the Sahyadri</b> it gives wood natural tourist and valleys, gushing waterfalls, <b>historic caves,</b> and <b>scenic views</b>. The surrounding hills were the stronghold of the Maratha chiefs, who practiced <b>guerrilla warfare</b> from here, against the Moghuls and later the British. Lonavala is now home to the houses of celebrities and business people, plus a host of resorts. Its other famous cousin town, <b>Khandala</b> lies just 5 km.</p>








